WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.570
- Is working in consulting glamorous?

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.530
This is the topic that I
wanna talk about today.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.410
Many people seem to believe
that working in consulting

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.350
and especially at an MBB consulting firm,

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.180
so McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.540
is a work that is attached
to a certain lifestyle,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.330
to a glamorous lifestyle indeed.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.023
Today I'm going to discuss exactly this,

00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:23.200
so welcome to another coffee break

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.250
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.320
My name is Heinrich.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.330
I'm a former McKinsey consultant.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.210
I spent six years with the firm

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.210
and now I'm in a CTO position
at a German retailer.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.000
And so before I jump
into the glamorous aspect

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.020
of the life of a consultant,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.850
I first of all wanna give
credits to this other video

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.330
from RocketBlocks that
I took as inspiration

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:46.540
and then also give two
important caveats to this video.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.270
And the first is that
the situation changes

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.810
quite significantly,
not only firm by firm,

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.780
but also among the different
geographies and countries.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.030
So to better understand what
is possible in your location

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.060
and your country,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.890
make sure that you do talk
to some local consultants

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:03.950
to really understand this.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.590
And the second caveat that I
wanna give is that this video

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.030
is not talking about one specific firm,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.000
but rather describing the
situation at MBB firms,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.750
so McKinsey, BCG, Bain.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.590
Another thing I just wanna be
clear on is that, of course,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.150
if you work in consulting,

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.750
you do not do it just for
these glamorous aspects.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.010
Trust me that you will not be happy,

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.270
you will not be satisfied with your job

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.150
if this is your main motivation.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.270
But of course, this
might be a little extra,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.580
this might be a little plus
that just makes your life

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.150
a little bit more comfortable.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.700
And of course, to some extent,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.210
this is also at least part of the appeal

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.810
of joining one of these firms.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.170
In the very end of the video,

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.830
we'll talk about another
very important topic.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.710
And this is why, even though
the life can be glamorous

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.590
in all these ways, in
practice, in reality,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.870
often these things are not possible.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.610
Often, you cannot really make
use of all of these things.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.700
So watch until the end for
this very important aspect

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.050
just to get the full
picture, the whole picture,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.630
to what extent the life of a consultant

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:04.210
is really glamorous.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.430
So let's get started.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.007
Let's start with travel.

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:09.760
And one of the aspects that
for sure most people find

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.670
most appealing is the
airline status that you get.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.390
For sure, with your national
airline, but with many others,

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.770
you will collect status.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:20.030
Almost every consultant I
know who works at an MBB firm

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.810
has a Senator status with
the German Lufthansa,

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.470
which corresponds to Star
Alliance Gold status.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.250
I even know a couple of
people who have a HON status

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.530
at the German Lufthansa.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.610
And for those of you who
do not know what that is,

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.032
it's just a status that gives you access

00:02:33.032 --> 00:02:35.010
to insane benefits.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.080
If you're interested in that,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.480
check out the Lufthansa page
to understand this better.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.110
And of course, what's
also important to say

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.870
is that this video will
especially focus on the situation

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.940
how it was until 2019.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.040
So before this new
situation in 2020 evolved,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.570
which of course, severely
impacts many of the things

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.760
that we are going to talk about.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.550
So this airline status is great.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.320
It gives you access to lots of lounges.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.200
This gives you access
to priority boarding.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.530
You collect lots of points.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.690
Another nice benefit is
that you will get access

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.070
to business class travel,

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.140
not only on long-haul flights,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.520
but at least for some
offices, for some firms,

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.600
even on short domestic flights.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.090
This is, of course, a perk
that is very comfortable,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.930
especially given that
you will fly quite a lot,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.200
in most countries at least.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.080
Similar to the airlines is the hotels.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.860
Here just have a collection
of some of the bonus cards

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.610
that I collected over the last years.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.650
Of course, there were many more

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.930
because most of them are digital nowadays.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.100
But it is true that you do get access

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.580
to lots of nice hotels.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.550
You will stay in Hyatts, in Ritz Carltons,

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:34.450
in Ws and all these nice Starwood hotels.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.480
And of course, it does make a difference,

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.210
if you really work super late,

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.030
if you really sit in the team
room until after midnight,

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.490
if then at least you come to a nice hotel.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.720
At least, I often felt that
this did increase team morale.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.520
So this is one of these nice perks

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.900
and these nice benefits
of working in consulting.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.690
Next point on travel is cars.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.050
So pretty much wherever you go,

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.910
you can pretty much always take the taxi.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.710
You never need to take public transport.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.350
And if you do need a rental car,

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.550
you often get access to nice cars,

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.390
which might make your
life easier this way.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.187
Next point is team activities.

00:04:05.187 --> 00:04:08.260
The one thing, of course, to
talk about is team dinners.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.330
So often after some nice
milestones in the project,

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.470
the partner will invite the whole team

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:15.790
to a nice, very upscale restaurant,

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.970
often also Michelin-star restaurants.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.910
Depending on what city
and area you are in,

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.500
you might eat in some of
the nicest restaurants

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.700
of the country.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.340
It's, of course, great to
have access to this nice food,

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.750
especially if you are a foodie
and appreciate it a lot.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.040
But besides dinners, often
you have also different

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.882
other types of offsite activities

00:04:32.882 --> 00:04:35.890
where your team, your
office, or maybe some groups

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.310
within the office meet for a weekend

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.040
or for some days throughout the week

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.210
to discuss some topics,
just have a offsite,

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.090
take some days off your regular work.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.839
Again, these are often great locations

00:04:45.839 --> 00:04:48.640
with great benefits, great activities,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.440
often nice night outs
afterwards in the evening.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.860
These are experiences where
you can form great memories

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.960
and build some lasting friendships also

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.350
beyond your daily job as a consultant.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:02.060
The next area I wanna talk
about is the compensation,

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.000
other benefits, that you
will get as a consultant.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.820
It is no secret that as an MBB consultant,

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.260
you will earn very decent salaries.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.850
And these high salaries, of course,

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.750
open up possibilities for you.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.870
You will be able to afford nicer things,

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.740
maybe a nicer, larger flat,

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.550
and whatever else you might fancy.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.150
Of course, if you are a regular
watcher of this channel,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.130
you do know that I advocate
not spending your whole money

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.400
but rather saving.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.780
I made a whole video
about why I do believe

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.870
it is so crucial to get
your savings rate high

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:32.890
as a consultant.

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.120
I will link it somewhere
above here, so check it out

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.350
to learn more about my
thinking on this topic.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.610
Similar to that is the car policies.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.770
So most MBB firms in
most locations do offer

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.470
a quite attractive car policy.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.900
So this means that even
as a junior consultant,

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.900
you will get access to nice cars.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.240
And the more senior you become,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.030
the larger the car that you could get.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.020
So here again, personally,
I did not make use

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.170
of this car policy.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.600
I decided not to take a company car.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.450
Often, then there are some
alternatives you can choose from

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.960
if you decide not to take it.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.910
For me, again, in this period of saving,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.000
the reason was to avoid the taxes

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.360
that you do need to pay if you get a car.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.740
But if you decide that you
wanna get a car anyway,

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:14.110
of course, the company car
policy is often very attractive

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:16.320
and can get you access
to some very nice cars.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.500
So these are the reasons
that in my perception

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.620
most contribute to this
maybe glamorous lifestyle

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.320
that you might get in such
an MBB consulting firm

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.840
in McKinsey, BCG or Bain.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.030
Of course, these things are subjective.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.690
So whether you do actually
perceive these things

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.900
to be glamorous, of course,

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.070
depends on your very personal opinion.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.530
And of course, there is
also an argument to be made

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.280
that these things that might
be perceived as glamorous

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.380
are the very same things that contribute

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.740
to the bad lifestyle,

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:46.000
that contribute to you spending
lots of time away from home.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.860
And of course, there's a
good argument to be made

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.690
that there's nothing more luxurious,

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.490
nothing more glamorous,
to spending time at home,

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.150
spending time with your family,

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.320
and I completely understand
that and completely see

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.267
where you're coming from if
this is what your opinion is.

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:00.400
But in the beginning I said that often,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.770
you actually cannot
really make use of this.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.050
I believe this is really
an important point

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.600
that you need to be aware of if you decide

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.630
to get into consulting
and maybe you believe

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.910
that you will have all
these benefits and perks.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.010
And this reason is that often your project

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:16.616
actually does not take place
in one of these large cities

00:07:16.616 --> 00:07:20.030
where you have these nice
hotels, nice airports.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.580
So it does happen that
your project is in a city

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.610
that's very small somewhere
in the middle of nowhere.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:28.850
Then the logistics are quite
complicated to get there.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:32.120
Often in these areas, there
just aren't any nice hotels.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.790
You just need to take
whatever hotel is available.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.450
And the airport might be so small

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.740
that you actually just cannot
fly there business class

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.190
because there are only low-cost carriers.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.370
So all of this is part of the reality

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:45.010
of being a consultant as well.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.090
And again, what I believe
is also very important

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:50.090
to clearly say is that the
smaller the consulting firm is

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:50.940
that you work for,

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.340
so if you work for tier two
or tier three consulting firm,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.950
and also if you work for Big
4 firm or a boutique firm,

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.360
these glamorous aspects often go away.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.430
So with these firms, you
will often not be able

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.510
to fly business class.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.897
These firms will often allow
you only to stay in hotel

00:08:05.897 --> 00:08:09.220
one or two tiers below the
hotels that I was talking about.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.080
So be aware that the firm that you join

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.068
will significantly impact your abilities

00:08:13.068 --> 00:08:15.220
to tap into all these perks.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.630
So what does my life look like now?

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.940
The truth is now that
I'm out of consulting

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.640
for about a year, most of
my statuses have expired.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.170
I'm not having access
to all of these things.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:27.820
Now personally, I take the bicycle.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.800
I still don't have a car
and I usually take the train

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:31.800
instead of a plane.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.290
And I must say that while
I, of course, enjoyed

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.480
all these nice perks while
I still lived in consulting,

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.560
I still also feel pretty
good given that now all

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.510
of these things have
been taken away from me.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.570
This is, I believe, also
an important takeaway

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:44.403
out of all of this.

00:08:44.403 --> 00:08:46.830
So while all of this, of course, is nice,

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.240
this is by no means necessary
and I do not really think

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:53.080
that this really improved
the quality of my life.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.260
So let me know your
opinion in the comments.

